From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:03:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] layersurface: Know the output while subclasses are
 constructed

wl-output was a plain property, so GObject set it only after
constructed() had run. The lock screen asks for its output there to put
its background on the same one, got NULL and created the background
without an output. The compositor then picks one itself: with a second
screen and the pointer on it, the background landed there, stacking it
below the lock screen failed with "Layer surface not on same output"
and phoc dropped phosh, again on every restart since phosh starts
locked. As a construct property the output is set before constructed().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/layersurface.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/layersurface.c b/src/layersurface.c
index e33cbd22..543990cb 100644
--- a/src/layersurface.c
+++ b/src/layersurface.c
@@ -478,7 +478,7 @@ phosh_layer_surface_class_init (PhoshLayerSurfaceClass *klass)
    */
   props[PROP_WL_OUTPUT] =
     g_param_spec_pointer ("wl-output", "", "",
-                          G_PARAM_READWRITE | G_PARAM_STATIC_STRINGS);
+                          G_PARAM_READWRITE | G_PARAM_CONSTRUCT | G_PARAM_STATIC_STRINGS);
   /**
    * PhoshLayerSurface:anchor:
    *
